"baseline_margin": 2.99, "analyst_adjustment": -1.49, "key_factors": ["Polling average shows Jackson narrowly ahead, roughly D+1 to D+2, with high-quality polls split", "Expert ratings split between Tossup and Lean D, with several outlets calling it a flip opportunity", "Prediction markets price Jackson around 57-58%, modestly favoring Democrats", "Late-September headlines show Jackson on defense over Gaza remarks and a PAC story, while Collins leads among swing voters"], "rationale": "Recent polls put Jackson slightly ahead, and several expert raters and prediction markets tilt toward a Democratic flip, but the race sits within a point or two and Collins retains incumbency advantages and strength with swing voters. Jackson's late gaffes temper what the polling alone would suggest, leaving a narrow Democratic edge.", "watch": "Whether Jackson's apology stops the damage from the Gaza remarks and PAC story, and whether Collins consolidates her lead among older and swing voters.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Susan Collins (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Maine's Senate race is one of the closest contests of the cycle, with four-term incumbent Susan Collins defending her seat against Maine Senate President Troy Jackson. The state leans Democratic by about four points, and the national environment favors Democrats, but Collins has repeatedly outperformed her party in Maine. Polling in late September shows Jackson ahead by roughly one to two points on average, though individual surveys range from a Collins lead to a nine-point Jackson advantage. Expert raters are split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets give Jackson about a 57-58% chance.\n\nThe race tightened after Jackson apologized for comments about Jewish Mainers' views on Gaza and faced questions about a PAC he previously ran, while Collins has shown strength with swing and older voters. Collins also holds a large fundraising edge. The contest remains genuinely competitive heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7341, "margin": 3.16}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6906, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.626, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6915, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5751, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6364, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6474, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6668, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6495, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6328, "margin": 1.5}]}